    "input": "search_query: Dear Northwind Outdoor Support Team,\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I am writing to respectfully inquire about a recent issue regarding my return of a high-end mountain bike. I recently attempted to return the item, but I was informed that a 15% restocking fee would be applied because the packaging was slightly damaged during my handling. I was quite surprised by this, as I had taken great care to ensure the bike itself remained in perfect, unused condition, and I had assumed the fee only applied if the product itself was compromised.\n\nAdditionally, I encountered a significant difficulty with the delivery process. The package was left at the depot, and I was unable to collect it within the required 48-hour window due to an unexpected family emergency. I understand that items priced over $500 require a signature and strict collection times, but I was not clearly notified of this specific deadline upon purchase. Could you please advise if there is any flexibility in these policies given the circumstances? I would greatly appreciate your guidance on how to proceed.\n\nThank you for your time and assistance.\n\nSincerely,\nArthur",
